// RS_VR_Unified -- one key section.
//
// BUG FIXED HERE. Both source packages opened with the SAME line:
//
//     addkeysection "RS HardPoints" RSHardPoints
//
// byte-identical in RS_Holsters/KEYCONF:1 and RS_HardPoints/KEYCONF:1 -- a
// copy-paste survivor of the 2026-08-23 split that was never renamed on the
// Holsters side. Two packages declaring one section id means they share a
// section file, and the binds of whichever loaded first get overwritten on
// every config save. That has been quietly eating one mod's key binds since
// the split. Merged, there is one section and the problem cannot recur.
addkeysection "RS VR Unified" RSVRUnified

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- grip
// The engine synthesises F13 (main hand) / F14 (off hand) for an anchor-context
// grip, ONLY when the grip arbiter resolves a clean tap that started inside an
// anchor's radius. Outside one, or during a combo, grip keeps its normal
// meaning and these never fire -- which is why binding grip's anchor role here
// does not steal grip from two-hand stabilize or the modifier layer.
//
// BOTH alias pairs below fire the SAME netevent, which every handler receives.
// In the separate pk3s that split existed because a key binds to exactly ONE
// alias, so two packages could not both claim F13. Merged, that constraint is
// gone and ONE bind is enough -- binding F13 to rs_holster_main alone already
// reaches the hardpoint manager too. Both names are kept so existing binds in
// an already-written config keep working; bind either, not both.
//
// NO DEFAULT BINDS -- bind these yourself under Customize Controls.
//
// STILL UNSOLVED, AND IT IS NOT A KEYCONF PROBLEM: the two managers arbitrate
// purely on "your hand is only ever in one place", which nothing enforces.
// Edit mode lets you drag a wrist mount onto a hip holster, and the engine
// emits one indistinguishable pulse for both contexts. Overlap the anchors and
// both doSwap bodies run on one press. The fix belongs in ZScript (a tiebreak
// on HolsterClaim*/HardpointClaim*, both already published every tic), not here.
addmenukey "Anchor: store/draw (MAIN hand)" rs_holster_main
alias rs_holster_main "netevent rs-vrhp-grab-main"

addmenukey "Anchor: store/draw (OFF hand)" rs_holster_off
alias rs_holster_off "netevent rs-vrhp-grab-off"

alias rs_hardpoint_main "netevent rs-vrhp-grab-main"
alias rs_hardpoint_off  "netevent rs-vrhp-grab-off"

